From: Jeremy Roman <jbroman@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:00:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] [M156] Serialize cross-world references in their source
 realm

Original change's description:
> Serialize cross-world references in their source realm
>
> Cross-world structured cloning previously entered the destination
> context before serializing the value. Certain proxy traps, error stack
> formatting, and other controllable behavior could therefore leak
> references to the destination realm back to the source world.
>
> Record the source ScriptState on cross-world references, and enter both
> its context and backup incumbent scope during serialization before
> switching to the destination context for unpacking and deserialization.
> Also fail closed on detached contexts, enforce target SharedArrayBuffer
> transfer eligibility, and guard promise settlement against synchronous
> context detachment during value conversion.
>
> Fixed: 584758944
